  <p>Vocele's plans cost $14.99, $29.99 or $49.99 a month. Every plan meters spoken conversation and pronunciation scoring by the month: Core includes 150 minutes of talk and 30 of pronunciation scoring, and the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> lists the rest.</p>

  <h2>Which one should you pick</h2>

  <p><strong>Speak</strong> is the better choice if you're a beginner who wants a fixed path, you're learning Korean or Chinese, or you practice on Android or the web.</p>

  <p>Pick <strong>Vocele</strong> if Speak's course has started repeating itself, you want feedback that shows where your sentence broke, you want the words from today's conversation back next week, or you're learning German, Portuguese, Russian or Polish.</p>

  <p>If pronunciation is your main goal, the <a href="/vs/elsa">ELSA Speak comparison</a> and <a href="/vs/boldvoice">the BoldVoice comparison</a> fit better than this one. If the real choice is between an app and a private tutor, I price Vocele against tutoring at $200 to $320 a month, and <a href="/blog/ai-speaking-coach-vs-human-tutor">the AI coach vs human tutor comparison</a> covers where apps lose.</p>

  <p>Vocele isn't on the App Store yet. If open conversation, corrections in your own sentence and words that come back are what you came for, <a href="/pricing">see the plans and the 3-day trial</a>. I'll update this page when the listing goes live.</p>
